   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#0"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Toungoo dynasty ruled Burma until 1752.",
   "chunk": 0,
   "date_text": "1752",
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#0"
  },
  {
   "text": "Tabinshwehti and Bayinnaung reunified the territories of the Pagan Kingdom for the first time since 1287.",
   "chunk": 0,
   "date_text": "1287",
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#0"
  },
  {
   "text": "The largest empire in the history of Southeast Asia collapsed in the 18 years following Bayinnaung's death in 1581.",
   "chunk": 1,
   "date_text": "1581",
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [
    "name_not_in_page:Bayinnaung's"
   ],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#1"
  },
  {
   "text": "Nyaungyan Min and his son Anaukpetlun succeeded in restoring a smaller kingdom by 1622.",
   "chunk": 2,
   "date_text": "1622",
   "date": null,
   "approximate": true,
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [
    "approximate_date"
   ],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#2"
  },
  {
   "text": "Starting from the 1720s, the kingdom was beset with raids by the Meitei people of the Chindwin River.",
   "chunk": 4,
   "date_text": "the 1720s",
   "date": null,
   "approximate": true,
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [
    "approximate_date"
   ],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#4"
  },
  {
   "text": "Raids by the Meitei intensified in the 1730s.",
   "chunk": 4,
   "date_text": "the 1730s",
   "date": null,
   "approximate": true,
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [
    "approximate_date"
   ],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#4"
  },
  {
   "text": "In 1740, the Mon people in Lower Burma began a rebellion, founding the Restored Hanthawaddy Kingdom.",
   "chunk": 4,
   "date_text": "1740",
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#4"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Hanthawaddy armies captured Inwa in 1752 and ended the 266-year-old Toungoo dynasty.",
   "chunk": 4,
   "date_text": "1752",
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#4"
  },
  {
   "text": "King Mingyi Nyo founded the First Taungoo Dynasty at Taungoo.",
   "chunk": 5,
   "date_text": "1485",
   "date": "1485",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 1,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#5"
  },
  {
   "text": "The First Taungoo Dynasty ended.",
   "chunk": 5,
   "date_text": "1599",
   "date": "1599",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 1,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#5"
  },
  {
   "text": "King Mingyi Nyo founded the First Taungoo Dynasty towards the end of the Ava Kingdom.",
   "chunk": 5,
   "date_text": "1510",
   "date": "1510",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 1,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#5"
  },
  {
   "text": "Inwa was conquered by the Mohnyin-led Shan sawbwas.",
   "chunk": 5,
   "date_text": "1527",
   "date": "1527",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 1,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#5"
  },
  {
   "text": "Tabinshwehti was crowned as king of all Burma at the ancient capital of Bagan.",
   "chunk": 6,
   "date_text": "1544",
   "date": "1544",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 1,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#6"
  },
  {
   "text": "Tabinshwehti was again defeated in the Burmese–Siamese War (1547–49).",
   "chunk": 8,
   "date_text": "1547",
   "date": "1547",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 1,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#8"
  },
  {
   "text": "Tabinshwehti was assassinated.",
   "chunk": 9,
   "date_text": "1550",
   "date": "1550",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 1,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#9"
  },
  {
   "text": "Bayinnaung succeeded to the throne",
   "chunk": 10,
   "date_text": "1550",
   "date": "1550",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#10"
  },
  {
   "text": "Bayinnaung launched a campaign of conquest invading several states, including Manipur",
   "chunk": 10,
   "date_text": "1560",
   "date": "1560",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#10"
  },
  {
   "text": "Bayinnaung launched a campaign of conquest invading several states, including Ayutthaya",
   "chunk": 10,
   "date_text": "1564",
   "date": "1564",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#10"
  },
  {
   "text": "Bayinnaung died",
   "chunk": 10,
   "date_text": "1581",
   "date": "1581",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#10"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Toungoo rulers withdrew from southern Burma and founded a second dynasty at Ava, the Nyaungyan or Restored Taungoo Dynasty.",
